+# Backend
+
+The workflows product's Django backend: the HogFlow serializer and viewsets, the services, models, providers and tasks behind them, and the facade the rest of PostHog uses.
+
+## invariants
+- graph-validation-has-one-door: Only presentation/views/hog_flow.py imports presentation/views/graph_validation.py.
+  protects: products/workflows/backend/presentation/views/graph_validation.py
+  chokepoint: products/workflows/backend/presentation/views/hog_flow.py
+  because: every graph write goes through HogFlowSerializer, so the editor, the API and MCP share one validate_graph; a second importer is a second write path that can skip or fork the check. import-linter's "presentation must use facade" contract is credited, but it only limits what presentation imports: it does not stop services/ or facade/ from importing the validator, which this chokepoint does
+  refuted: coherence run staged a sibling module re-exporting graph_validation's _branch_slot_count -> the check classified it a bypass; graded checker-choked by import-linter (2026-09-30)
+  kinds: none
+- server-compiles-all-bytecode: Under products/workflows/backend only presentation/views/hog_flow.py imports a bytecode compiler.
+  over: every non-test Python file under products/workflows/backend; create_bytecode, compile_filters_expr and generate_template_bytecode are allowed only in presentation/views/hog_flow.py, the paved path
+  via: lint ruff:TID251 matching "server-compiles-all-bytecode"
+  because: client-supplied bytecode is discarded on every write path and the serializer recompiles it, so a compiler call anywhere else is a second compile path that can drift from the serializer or trust client input
+  refuted: staged services/coherence_break_bytecode.py importing create_bytecode -> ruff TID251 went red at its line 1 with this invariant's message (2026-09-30)
+  kinds: none
+- ses-only-through-provider: Under products/workflows/backend only providers/ses.py imports boto3 or botocore; everything else calls SESProvider.
+  over: every non-test Python file under products/workflows/backend; boto3 and botocore are allowed only in providers/ses.py, the paved path
+  via: lint ruff:TID251 matching "ses-only-through-provider"
+  because: SESProvider owns the client config (timeouts, retries), the typed stubs and the error mapping, as review asked in #89643; a raw boto3 client in a task or service bypasses all three, and facade/api.py keeps boto3 off the facade import path on purpose
+  refuted: staged tasks/coherence_break_boto3.py importing boto3 -> ruff TID251 went red at its line 1 with this invariant's message (2026-09-30)
+  kinds: none
